{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a Shopify FAQ accordion section.
    
    Layout:
    - Single column
    - Accordion style only
    
    Settings:
    - Background gradient picker
    - Font picker
    - Icon style selector (+ / -)
    - Animation toggle (smooth expand)
    - Only one item open at a time (toggle)
    
    FAQ CONTENT:
    
    Membership:
    What is Entitled?
    A members-only storefront for curated, limited-quantity clothing — top-tier quality, always.
    
    Is membership paid?
    No. Membership is free and granted through approval.
    
    How do I become a member?
    Apply with your details. Approval is typically granted within 10–15 days.
    
    Can I shop without membership?
    No. If you are not a member, you cannot access the store.
    
    Who is a customer?
    Only members. If you are not a member, you are not a customer.
    
    What details do you collect for membership?
    Name, mobile number, email address, and shipping address.
    
    What do members get?
    Membership is the customer identity. It grants store access and members-first support.
    
    Products:
    How is access priced?
    Pricing reflects member access, verification, and availability.
    
    Are the products authentic?
    Yes. We handpick from select authentic channels and verify quality before listing.
    
    Do you sell factory rejects or quality rejects?
    No. Items that fail our quality standard are not listed.
    
    Drops:
    Are drops restocked?
    By default, no. Drops open and close. When they close, they become archive.
    
    Shipping & Returns:
    What is your return policy?
    No-questions-asked returns, subject to basic condition verification and fair use. Approved returns are issued as store credits only.
    
    Support:
    Do you have purchase limits?
    No purchase limits at this time. Limits may be introduced later if needed.
    
    How can I contact support?
    WhatsApp customer support (details on the website). Members-first resolution.
    
{% enddoc %}
{% assign ai_gen_id = block.id | replace: '_', '' | downcase %}

{% style %}
  .ai-faq-accordion-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: block;
    width: {{ block.settings.desktop_width_percent }}%;
    max-width: 100%;
    padding: {{ block.settings.section_padding }}px 20px;
    background: {{ block.settings.background_gradient }};
    font-family: {{ block.settings.font_family.family }}, {{ block.settings.font_family.fallback_families }};
    font-weight: {{ block.settings.font_family.weight }};
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__container-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__item-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    border-bottom: 1px solid {{ block.settings.border_color }};
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__item-{{ ai_gen_id }}:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__header-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 100%;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: {{ block.settings.item_padding }}px 0;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-align: left;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__question-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    flex: 1;
    font-size: {{ block.settings.question_font_size }}px;
    font-weight: {{ block.settings.question_font_weight }};
    color: {{ block.settings.question_color }};
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: {{ block.settings.icon_size }}px;
    height: {{ block.settings.icon_size }}px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: {{ block.settings.icon_color }};
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }

  {% if block.settings.enable_animation %}
    .ai-faq-accordion__icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      transition: transform 0.3s ease;
    }
  {% endif %}

  .ai-faq-accordion__item-{{ ai_gen_id }}.active .ai-faq-accordion__icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    {% if block.settings.icon_style == 'plus' %}
      transform: rotate(45deg);
    {% else %}
      transform: rotate(180deg);
    {% endif %}
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__content-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    {% if block.settings.enable_animation %}
      transition: max-height 0.3s ease, padding 0.3s ease;
    {% endif %}
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__item-{{ ai_gen_id }}.active .ai-faq-accordion__content-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-height: 1000px;
    padding-bottom: {{ block.settings.item_padding }}px;
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__answer-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.answer_font_size }}px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: {{ block.settings.answer_color }};
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__category-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.category_font_size }}px;
    font-weight: {{ block.settings.category_font_weight }};
    color: {{ block.settings.category_color }};
    margin: {{ block.settings.category_spacing }}px 0 {{ block.settings.item_padding }}px 0;
    padding-top: {{ block.settings.category_spacing }}px;
    border-top: 2px solid {{ block.settings.category_border_color }};
  }

  .ai-faq-accordion__category-{{ ai_gen_id }}:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: none;
  }
{% endstyle %}

